{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS6t5Ua1oxNcEcsh18LT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: a `save_fact` now writes only the new fact to the cache, about 20 tokens, instead of the whole ~1050-token system prompt. I haven't run it against the real API. I only checked it with a local simulation of the caching rules (described below).\n\n**Cause.** The whole system prompt was one text block, and the long-term facts sat in the middle of it, with the `Language` line after them. The cache only reuses an exactly matching start of the request, so any new fact changed the whole block and the full prompt was written to the cache again. This already happened on round 2 of the same message, because `save_fact` adds the fact before the next request is built.\n\n**What I changed in `bot.py`:**\n- **Split the prompt into blocks, from stable to changing:** instructions, then the profile (date, name, zones, goal, language), then one block per fact. Nothing comes after the facts.\n- **Cache markers on two blocks:** on the last fact and on the profile. When a fact is added, the earlier blocks stay the same. The API looks back over earlier block boundaries (about 20 blocks) and finds the entry the previous request saved. The marker on the profile is a fallback in case that lookback misses.\n- **`save_fact` only appends now:** it ignores empty facts and exact duplicates. A comment in `build_system` explains why facts must not be reordered or edited in place.\n- I also updated the caching paragraph in the README.\n\n**Check.** I ran the real `reply()` loop with a fake model that applies the same caching rules. The round right after `save_fact` reads about 1140–1220 tokens from cache and writes 18–20. Before the change, it wrote about 1050–1100. `data/athletes.json` and `logs/usage.jsonl` are unchanged. After you deploy, check `logs/usage.jsonl`: on the call after a `save_fact`, `cache_creation_input_tokens` should be a few dozen tokens.\n\n**Two limits:**\n- **Keyword tool filtering still resets the cache.** Tools come before the system prompt in the request, so a message that adds the planning or race tools rewrites everything (the 1305 and 1334 lines in the log). `NOTES.md` says to keep the filtering, so I left it.\n- **The profile fallback may not take effect.** Sonnet 4.5 only caches a prefix of at least 1024 tokens. By my estimate, the tools plus instructions plus profile come to just under that. Then that marker does nothing (it doesn't cause an error). The main mechanism, the marker on the last fact, isn't affected by this.\n\nThe full write-up is in `ANSWER.md`. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3219,"cache_read_input_tokens":37104,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3219},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b34ac5c-3132-4024-bd58-874a3005a084","uuid":"ed3752e2-5ea4-4169-80c4-1df91b7f49dc","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:22:01.862Z","request_id":"req_011CgS6t5ESHqiuT2cufwFbZ"}
